course: dictionary
lesson: 3070
title: Ed: a school word, a name, and the past
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: The word «ed» has several meanings, and the context tells you which one you need. «Phys ed» is short for physical education, the PE lesson, and «2nd ed.» in a book means second edition. «Ed.» with a full stop usually means editor or edition.
explain: Ed is also a boy's name, short for Edward, Edmund or Edwin. A capital letter and a person in the sentence are your clues. The ending -ed is different again: it is added to regular verbs to make the past, so play becomes played, and cry becomes cried.
fact: «Ed» in school usually means education, as in «phys ed» (physical education).
fact: «ed.» with a full stop means editor or edition: «3rd ed.» is the third edition of a book.
fact: Ed is a boy's name, short for Edward, Edmund or Edwin.
fact: «-ed» is added to regular verbs to make the past: jump becomes jumped, want becomes wanted.
fact: The ending -ed sounds like /t/ in jumped, /d/ in played and /id/ in wanted.
exercise: «The class had phys ed before lunch.» What does ed mean in phys ed? | The past tense of a verb | A boy called Ed | An editor who checks a book | *Education, a school subject
exercise: «Ed and Ella went to the park.» What is Ed here? | A school subject | An editor of a book | *A boy's name, short for Edward | The past tense of a verb
exercise: Which verb is regular and adds -ed to make the past? | swim | run | *jump | go
test: «3rd ed.» on the cover of a book means: | *The third edition of the book | A boy named Edward | The past tense of edit | Education for three years
test: Which is the correct past tense of cry? | crying | cryed | *cried | cries
exam: In «jumped», what does the -ed show? | *That the jump happened in the past | Education in school | A boy's name | An edition of a book
